kunzite: Adreno 710 step 20, the zap shader, gen7_start and the CP started (kgpu=20; the port map's 19-20).
20 runs with GX on and the GPU's context, ring and microcode from step 19. The zap shader as
kgsl_zap_shader_load does it (qcom_mdt_load + PAS_AUTH_AND_RESET): a710_zap.mdt's loadable
segments (mdt_phdr_valid: PT_LOAD, not the hash, memsz != 0; one here, relocatable, 0x1000 +
0x79c) give PAS_MEM_SETUP(13, 0x89e1a000, 0x1000) - INIT_IMAGE was step 12's in this run - then
each segment is copied from the .mdt or its .bNN file (a710_zap.b01, uploaded to
/usr/share/firmware/kunzite) to the FDT region (uncached, words), the rest zeroed, then
PAS_AUTH_AND_RESET(13). Not undone (kgsl never unloads it; TrustZone holds the region). Then
gen7_start for gen7_3_0 in kgsl's order: GBIF client QoS 3, UCHE GBIF/trap/write-through/GMEM
range (16M + 512K)/ways/CMDQ, the NC_MODE_CNTLs (highest bank bit 15, min access 32, UBWC 4.0),
UCHE mode, hang detect 0xcfffff, UCHE client PF, RB_CMP_DBG_ECO bit 11, the GMU power counters,
CP_PROTECT_CNTL 0xb and the 46 gen7_0_0_protected_regs, CP_APRIV 0x6f, _set_secvid (TSB off,
trusted 0xf0000000 + 0xfffff000), the AO and gen7_3_0 clock gating tables and RBBM_CLOCK_CNTL
0x8aa8aa82; register blocks announced as a whole and read back. Then gen7_rb_start: RPTR_ADDR
(scratch page), RB_CNTL 0x20c, CP_SQE_CNTL 1 (the CP fetches the microcode through context 0),
gen7_cp_init_cmds at the ring's head (CP_THREAD_CONTROL bit 27; CP_ME_INIT mask 0x94b with an
empty power-up list in the scratch page, as upstream a7xx does), WPTR 10, then
adreno_spin_idle's test (RPTR 10, CX busy bit 23 clear) for up to 2 s; CP, RBBM and context 0
fault registers printed. Undo: CP_SQE_CNTL 0 first. Also: kgsl's trusted range starts at
0xf0000000, so step 19's GPU addresses move from 0x100000000 to 0xe0000000; step 18 maps the
whole 256K GPU block; kg_scm takes a third argument.

